[2026-03-14T22:58:32.825Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WWNYNXkVLuabXTYujVqDcY","type":"tool_result","content":"191:- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n203:#### Test: Sidebar Members link navigates correctly\n205:- **Action**: User clicks \"Members\" in the workspace section\n206:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/members`.\n279:- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n391:#### Test: Issue row status change updates group membership\n727:- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"Bob\" from the member selector\n861:#### Test: Assignee filter dropdown shows all team members\n862:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team \"Engineering\" has members Alice, Bob, and Charlie\n864:- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all team members with their avatars and names: Alice, Bob, Charlie, and an \"Unassigned\" option. Each option has a checkbox.\n1139:- **Initial state**: Issue is unassigned. The workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", and \"Charlie\".\n1141:- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown appears showing all workspace members with their avatars and names.\n1144:- **Initial state**: The assignee dropdown is open showing all members\n1297:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\", \"Carol Lee\".\n1301:#### Test: Assignee selector allows selecting a member\n1509:- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped by priority level (Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority). Each group has a collapsible header showing the priority icon and name. Changing to \"Assignee\" regroups by assigned team member.\n1675:- **Expected**: All 3 project cards are displayed on the page. Projects from all teams are shown regardless of team membership.\n1702:#### Test: Lead filter dropdown shows all workspace members\n1703:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\".\n1705:- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all workspace members with their avatars and names. Each option has a checkbox. A searchable input may be present to filter the member list.\n1751:- **Expected**: The modal displays the following fields: Name (text input, required), Description (text area), Status (dropdown), Lead (searchable member selector), Target date (date picker), Teams (multi-select). \"Create Project\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible at the bottom.\n1759:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\".\n1761:- **Expected**: The member list filters to show only \"Alice\". User can select \"Alice\" as the lead. The selected lead shows their avatar and name.\n1879:- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead is \"Jane Doe\". Workspace members include \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n1881:- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown opens listing all workspace members with avatars and names. \"Jane Doe\" is shown as currently selected.\n1889:- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead selector is open. Members: \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n1891:- **Expected**: Only \"Bob Jones\" appears in the filtered results. Other members are hidden.\n2106:## Members Page (`/settings/members`)\n2108:**Components**: MemberList, InviteMemberModal, MemberActions\n2110:### MemberList\n2112:#### Test: Members page renders with list of all workspace members\n2113:- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 members: Alice (Admin, Engineering team), Bob (Member, Engineering and Design teams), Carol (Member, Design team). User navigates to `/settings/members`.\n2114:- **Expected**: A list/table is displayed showing all 3 members. Each row shows the member's avatar, name, email, role badge (Admin or Member), and team badges. The \"Invite Member\" button is visible at the top of the page. The page title reads \"Members\".\n2116:#### Test: Member row displays avatar, name, email, role, and team badges\n2117:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member named \"Alice Smith\" with email \"alice@example.com\", role \"Admin\", belonging to \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" teams. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2118:- **Expected**: Alice's row displays her avatar (initials or image), full name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", an \"Admin\" role badge, and two team badges showing \"Engineering\" and \"Design\".\n2120:#### Test: Members list shows correct role badges with visual distinction\n2121:- **Initial state**: Workspace has members with Admin and Member roles. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2122:- **Expected**: Admin role badges are visually distinct from Member role badges (different color or styling). Admin badges clearly indicate elevated privileges.\n2124:#### Test: Members list shows team badges for each member\n2125:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member belonging to 3 teams (Engineering, Design, QA). User is on `/settings/members`.\n2126:- **Expected**: The member's row displays 3 team badges, one for each team. Each badge shows the team name.\n2128:#### Test: Members list shows member with no teams\n2129:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member who does not belong to any teams. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2130:- **Expected**: The member's row is displayed without any team badges. No error or placeholder is shown in the teams column.\n2132:#### Test: Members page shows empty state when no members exist\n2133:- **Initial state**: Workspace has only the current user (no other members). User is on `/settings/members`.\n2134:- **Expected**: The list shows only the current user. A friendly message or the invite button is prominently displayed to encourage adding members.\n2136:#### Test: Members list updates after inviting a new member\n2137:- **Initial state**: Workspace has 2 members. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2138:- **Action**: User invites a new member via the Invite Member modal (enters \"newuser@example.com\" and submits)\n2139:- **Expected**: The members list now shows 3 members including the newly invited member. The new member appears with their email and a default \"Member\" role.\n2141:#### Test: Members list updates after removing a member\n2142:- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 members. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2143:- **Action**: User removes one member via the remove action (confirms removal in the confirmation dialog)\n2144:- **Expected**: The members list now shows 2 members. The removed member is no longer visible in the list.\n2146:### InviteMemberModal\n2148:#### Test: Invite Member button opens invite modal\n2149:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`.\n2150:- **Action**: User clicks the \"Invite Member\" button\n2151:- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with a title (e.g., \"Invite Member\"), an email input field, a \"Send Invite\" (or \"Invite\") button, and a \"Cancel\" button. The modal has a backdrop overlay.\n2153:#### Test: Invite member with valid email\n2154:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open. Workspace has 2 existing members.\n2155:- **Action**: User enters \"newcolleague@example.com\" in the email field and clicks \"Send Invite\"\n2156:- **Expected**: The modal closes. A success message is shown (e.g., \"Invitation sent\" or the member appears in the list). The new member appears in the members list with email \"newcolleague@example.com\", role \"Member\", and no team badges.\n2158:#### Test: Invite member with invalid email format\n2159:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open.\n2160:- **Action**: User enters \"not-an-email\" in the email field and clicks \"Send Invite\"\n2161:- **Expected**: A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). The modal remains open. No member is added.\n2163:#### Test: Invite member with empty email field\n2164:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open.\n2165:- **Action**: User clicks \"Send Invite\" without entering an email\n2168:#### Test: Invite member with already existing email\n2169:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open. A member with email \"existing@example.com\" already exists in the workspace.\n2170:- **Action**: User enters \"existing@example.com\" in the email field and clicks \"Send Invite\"\n2171:- **Expected**: An error message is shown (e.g., \"This email is already a member of the workspace\"). The modal remains open. No duplicate member is created.\n2173:#### Test: Cancel invite member modal\n2174:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open and has typed \"someone@example.com\" in the email field.\n2176:- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new member is added to the workspace. The members list remains unchanged.\n2178:#### Test: Close invite modal by clicking backdrop\n2179:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open.\n2181:- **Expected**: The modal closes without sending an invite.\n2183:#### Test: Invite modal email field can be submitted via Enter key\n2184:- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open and has entered \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field.\n2186:- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Send Invite\". The new member is added if the email is valid.\n2188:#### Test: Invite member modal can be opened multiple times in sequence\n2189:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`.\n2190:- **Action**: User clicks \"Invite Member\", enters \"first@example.com\", clicks \"Send Invite\". Then clicks \"Invite Member\" again, enters \"second@example.com\", clicks \"Send Invite\".\n2191:- **Expected**: Both members are added to the workspace. The members list shows both new members. The modal opens cleanly with an empty email field the second time (no residual data from the first invite).\n2193:### MemberActions\n2195:#### Test: Change member role from Member to Admin\n2196:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member \"Bob\" with role \"Member\". Current user is an Admin. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2197:- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for Bob and selects \"Admin\"\n2198:- **Expected**: Bob's role is updated to \"Admin\". The role badge in Bob's row changes to \"Admin\" with the Admin styling. The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows Admin).\n2200:#### Test: Change member role from Admin to Member\n2201:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member \"Alice\" with role \"Admin\". Current user is an Admin. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2202:- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for Alice and selects \"Member\"\n2203:- **Expected**: Alice's role is updated to \"Member\". The role badge in Alice's row changes to \"Member\" with the Member styling.\n2205:#### Test: Role dropdown displays available roles\n2206:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. A member row is visible.\n2207:- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for a member\n2208:- **Expected**: A dropdown menu appears showing the available roles: \"Admin\" and \"Member\". The currently assigned role is visually indicated (checked, highlighted, or selected).\n2210:#### Test: Role dropdown can be used multiple times in sequence\n2211:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. A member \"Bob\" has role \"Member\".\n2212:- **Action**: User changes Bob's role to \"Admin\" via the dropdown. Then user changes Bob's role back to \"Member\" via the dropdown again.\n2213:- **Expected**: Bob's role first changes to \"Admin\", then back to \"Member\". Both changes are persisted correctly. The dropdown works correctly on the second use.\n2215:#### Test: Remove member button shows confirmation dialog\n2216:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. Workspace has a member \"Carol\".\n2218:- **Expected**: A confirmation dialog appears asking the user to confirm the removal (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to remove Carol from the workspace?\"). The dialog has \"Confirm\" (or \"Remove\") and \"Cancel\" buttons. The member is NOT removed yet.\n2220:#### Test: Confirm member removal deletes the member\n2221:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The removal confirmation dialog is open for member \"Carol\". Workspace has 3 members.\n2223:- **Expected**: The dialog closes. Carol is removed from the workspace. The members list now shows 2 members. Carol no longer appears in the list. The removal is persisted.\n2225:#### Test: Cancel member removal keeps the member\n2226:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The removal confirmation dialog is open for member \"Carol\".\n2228:- **Expected**: The dialog closes. Carol remains in the members list. No changes are made.\n2231:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The current user's row is visible.\n2234:#### Test: Cannot change your own role (or last Admin cannot be demoted)\n2235:- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The current user is the only Admin in the workspace.\n2236:- **Action**: User attempts to change their own role to \"Member\"\n2237:- **Expected**: Either the role dropdown is disabled for the current user's own row, or an error is shown (e.g., \"Cannot demote the last Admin\"). The workspace must always have at least one Admin.\n2239:#### Test: Removed member's issues remain assigned but member is gone from selectors\n2240:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member \"Carol\" who is assigned to 2 issues. User is on `/settings/members`.\n2242:- **Expected**: Carol is removed from the members list. The issues previously assigned to Carol retain their data but Carol no longer appears as a selectable assignee in issue forms or selectors.\n2251:- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 teams: \"Engineering\" (prefix ENG, 5 members, active cycle \"Sprint 10\"), \"Design\" (prefix DES, 3 members, no active cycle), \"QA\" (prefix QA, 2 members, active cycle \"QA Cycle 4\"). User navigates to `/settings/teams`.\n2252:- **Expected**: The page displays 3 team cards. Each card shows the team name, identifier prefix, member count, and active cycle name (if any). A \"Create Team\" button is visible at the top of the page. The page title reads \"Teams\".\n2262:#### Test: Team card displays member count\n2263:- **Initial state**: Workspace has a team \"Engineering\" with 5 members. User is on `/settings/teams`.\n2264:- **Expected**: The team card shows the member count as \"5 members\" (or similar text like \"5\" with a members icon).\n2277:- **Expected**: The user is navigated to the team settings view for \"Engineering\", showing editable fields for team name, description, identifier, and a section for managing team members.\n2286:- **Expected**: The teams page now shows 3 team cards, including the newly created \"QA\" team with its identifier prefix, a member count of 0 (or 1 if the creator is auto-added), and no active cycle.\n2333:- **Expected**: The modal closes. The teams page now shows the new \"Quality Assurance\" team card with prefix \"QA\", member count of 0 (or 1), and no active cycle. The team is persisted (reloading shows the team).\n2369:- **Expected**: The team settings view displays: Team name field showing \"Engineering\" (inline editable), Identifier prefix field showing \"ENG\" (inline editable), Description field showing \"Core engineering team\" (inline editable), and a \"Team Members\" section listing current members. A \"Back\" or navigation link to return to the teams list is visible. A \"Delete Team\" button is also present.\n2406:#### Test: Team members section lists all current team members\n2407:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2408:- **Expected**: The Team Members section displays a list of 3 members. Each member row shows their avatar and name. An \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n2410:#### Test: Add member to team via team settings\n2411:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 2 members. Workspace member \"David\" is not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2412:- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\", selects \"David\" from the member selector, and confirms\n2413:- **Expected**: David is added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members including David. The team card on the teams page reflects the updated member count. David's member row on the Members page (`/settings/members`) now includes an \"Engineering\" team badge.\n2415:#### Test: Add member selector shows only non-team members\n2416:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has members Alice and Bob. Workspace also has Carol and David who are not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2417:- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\"\n2418:- **Expected**: The member selector dropdown shows only Carol and David (members not already on the team). Alice and Bob are not shown in the dropdown since they are already team members.\n2420:#### Test: Remove member from team via team settings\n2421:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2422:- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to Carol's name in the Team Members list\n2423:- **Expected**: A confirmation prompt appears (e.g., \"Remove Carol from Engineering?\"). User confirms. Carol is removed from the team members list. The section now shows 2 members. Carol remains a workspace member but is no longer on the \"Engineering\" team. The team card member count decreases.\n2425:#### Test: Cancel remove member from team\n2426:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2427:- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to a member's name, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation prompt\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 150, offset: 0]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018GPwKEcD1FYpyKVFpeMfoq","session_id":"90024d97-e35b-4034-b06d-d2556c8f7f36","uuid":"f05de707-47ad-4559-bd63-e2717bd28fc2"}
